#  BreadBot v69 — ENVIRONMENT
#
#  ── THE AI POOL (v69) — add as many APIs as you want ──
#  Put a key in a numbered slot. The provider behind each key is
#  AUTO-DETECTED from the key shape:
#
#      AIza…        → Google Gemini
#      sk-or-v1-…   → OpenRouter
#      gsk_…        → Groq
#      sk-…         → OpenAI
#      anything else → Rewind (your current working endpoint)
#
#  Per-slot overrides (optional):
#      API_1_NAME=venice
#      API_1_URL=https://api.venice.ai/api/v1/chat/completions
#      API_1_MODEL=venice-uncensored
#
#  HOW IT SPLITS THE WORK: every task goes to the NEXT healthy
#  provider (round-robin). 1 working API = it does everything.
#  5 working APIs = the tasks split 5 ways. A provider that fails
#  twice goes on cooldown (5 min, doubling to 30 min) and a
#  background check every 5 min revives it automatically when it
#  answers again — top up a key, no restart needed.
